<TextPage
  title="Terms"
  eyebrow="Terms of use"
  heading="What AURA is, and is not"
  lede="AURA is a free information service. It summarises Nigerian business news about who owns and controls companies. Please read these points before relying on anything here."
  description="The terms for using AURA: an information service built from news reports, not legal or financial advice."
  updated="2026-11-07"
>
  <h2>Records come from news reports</h2>
  <p>
    Every ownership, board and contract record on AURA is drawn by software from articles published by news
    outlets. A record says that an outlet reported something. It is not a record from the Corporate Affairs
    Commission (CAC), it has not been checked against the CAC register, and it is not a finding that anyone
    did anything wrong. Reports can be mistaken, out of date, or about a different person with the same name.
  </p>

  <h2>Not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on AURA, or in the Morning Brief, is legal, financial, investment or compliance advice. Check the
    original reporting and the official registers, and take professional advice, before acting on it.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    AURA is provided as it is, without any promise that it is complete, accurate, current or always available.
    As far as the law allows, we are not responsible for loss caused by relying on it.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If something is wrong, tell us through the <a href={href("dispute/")}>dispute form</a>. Corrections are
    listed on the <a href={href("corrections/")}>corrections page</a>. How we handle personal data is set out in
    the <a href={href("privacy/")}>privacy notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    You are welcome to read, link to and quote AURA with credit to AURA and the original outlet. Please do not
    overload the site with automated requests, or present its records as official register data.
  </p>
</TextPage>
